iament but they're also saying  that the parliament isn't acting in the  people's interests and that's an  incredibly strong statement how will it  be received here we won't be expecting  people out on the streets we're going to  be expecting political reactions  cleric a key sheer cleric who has 73  members of parliament uh it's the  largest block he's got a lot to lose  here because he was riding on uh the  federal court dissolving poem because he  wanted to see new elections he'll have a  reaction the tashrin movement of people  that protested in October of 2020 and  had a change of government as a result  they'll have a reaction to this what  that's going to be we don't know had it  just been a normal decision where they  said it's not down to us it's not down  to the Supreme Court and left it at that  it may well have been been easier to  Stage manage but now the Supreme Court  has actually said to the parliament you  guys aren't representing the people and  that needs to be something that  Parliament will and has to react to  okay thank you for that Imran Khan there  for us in Baghdad
 

